---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Terms of Service: Using NameJoiner’s Free Name Tools';
const description =
  'Plain-English terms for NameJoiner’s free name tools: results are suggestions, not guaranteed available or trademark-safe, and use is at your own risk.';
const updated = 'September 19, 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/terms-of-service">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-8 pt-12 sm:px-6 sm:pt-16">
    <h1>Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: <time datetime="2026-09-19">{updated}</time></p>
    <div class="prose-body mt-5 text-lg">
      <p>By using NameJoiner.com you agree to these terms. They are written to be readable. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.</p>
    </div>

    <article class="prose-body mt-12 space-y-10">
      <section aria-labelledby="service">
        <h2 id="service" class="mb-3">What NameJoiner provides</h2>
        <p>NameJoiner offers free, rule-based tools that suggest names: couple names, baby names, business names, usernames, gamertags and nicknames. We may change, pause or remove any tool at any time without notice.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="suggestions">
        <h2 id="suggestions" class="mb-3">Results are starting points</h2>
        <p>Every name the tools produce is a suggestion, nothing more. We do not promise that a name is unique, that a domain, username or gamertag is available, that it is free of trademark or other legal claims, or that it suits your purpose or will not carry an unintended meaning in another language or culture. Tools that mention length or character limits for a platform describe them as we understand them, and platforms can change their rules.</p>
        <p>Before you rely on a name, check it yourself: search the domain registrar, the platform, and, for a business name, the trademark database and business registry of the country or state where you operate. If the name will carry real money, ask a qualified professional. Nothing on this site is legal, financial or professional advice.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="use">
        <h2 id="use" class="mb-3">Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>Please use the tools for lawful, ordinary purposes. Do not:</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>use the tools or their results to harass, impersonate or deceive anyone, or to infringe someone else’s rights;</li>
          <li>scrape the site in bulk, overload it, or try to disrupt or break into it;</li>
          <li>copy the site’s text, design or word lists and present them as your own.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">You are welcome to use the names you generate however you like, subject to the law and to any rights others may hold in a name.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="ip">
        <h2 id="ip" class="mb-3">Ownership</h2>
        <p>The site’s content, code, design and word lists belong to NameJoiner. Short, common name combinations are not something we claim to own, so we do not claim ownership of the specific names you generate.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="links">
        <h2 id="links" class="mb-3">Outside links</h2>
        <p>Some results link to other sites, such as a domain registrar or a social platform. We do not control those sites and are not responsible for their content, prices or policies. Any affiliate links will be labeled as such.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="warranty">
        <h2 id="warranty" class="mb-3">No warranty</h2>
        <p>The site and its tools are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind, express or implied. We do not guarantee that the site will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that the results will be accurate, appropriate or fit for a particular purpose. Nickname and baby-name results are filtered as carefully as we can, but a filter can miss things, so read each result before you use it, especially for children.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="liability">
        <h2 id="liability" class="mb-3">Limit of liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, NameJoiner and its owners are not liable for any loss or damage that comes from using, or being unable to use, the site or its results. That includes lost domains, rejected trademark applications, rebranding costs and lost income. Some places do not allow these limits, in which case they apply only as far as the law permits.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="changes">
        <h2 id="changes" class="mb-3">Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms and will change the date above when we do. Using the site after a change means you accept the new terms. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:hello@namejoiner.com">hello@namejoiner.com</a>. See also our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
